# git's "allowed signers" file for Kwal release tags (sshkeys(5) format).
#
# The public key below is the SSH key that also authenticates the maintainer on
# GitHub, so GitHub shows signed tags and the releases cut from them as
# "Verified". The point of keeping it in the tree is that verification does not
# depend on trusting the forge: check a tag with the key that came from the
# repository itself, over the same transport you fetched the code from.
#
#   git clone --branch v0.1.0 https://github.com/iguruspain/kwal.git
#   cd kwal
#   git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=docs/kwal_signers verify-tag v0.1.0
#
# Expected line on success:
#   Good "git" signature for iguruspain@localhost with ED25519 key SHA256:AVhMbpiC6AslgpBcLx6dJUiXbh8n2yIO8E22Bze9E2Y
#
# Signing side (maintainer, one-time repo config; scripts/release.sh refuses to
# cut a tag without it):
#   git config gpg.format ssh
#   git config user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile docs/kwal_signers
iguruspain@localhost namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHx4DpiLhj7TGjkeJ1BB4weaZrj7QZL3yO1HYdOt4/s4
